    "category": "Python Basics",
    "question_hi": "Kya Python ek compiled ya interpreted language hai?",
    "answer_hi": "> Python ko generally interpreted language mana jaata hai. Lekin, execution se pehle, Python source code ko bytecode (`.pyc`) mein compile karta hai. Yeh bytecode phir Python Virtual Machine (PVM) dwara execute hota hai. Toh, Python internally compilation aur interpretation dono use karta hai, lekin ise commonly interpreted language kaha jaata hai kyunki PVM bytecode ko execute karta hai, native machine code directly run karne ke bajaye.\r\n\r\n**Short version (30-second answer):**\r\n\r\n> Python ek interpreted language hai. Internally, yeh pehle source code ko bytecode mein compile karta hai, aur phir Python Virtual Machine (PVM) us bytecode ko interpret aur execute karta hai. Isi liye Python ko interpreted language kaha jaata hai, chahe yeh internally ek compilation step bhi perform karta ho.\r\n\r\nYeh version most interviewers expect karte hain.",
    "question_en": "Is Python a compiled or interpreted language?",
    "answer_en": "> Python is generally considered an interpreted language. However, before execution, Python first compiles the source code into bytecode (`.pyc`). This bytecode is then executed by the Python Virtual Machine (PVM). So, Python uses both compilation and interpretation internally, but it is commonly referred to as an interpreted language because the PVM executes the bytecode rather than running native machine code directly.\r\n\r\n**Short version (30-second answer):**\r\n\r\n> Python is an interpreted language. Internally, it first compiles the source code into bytecode, and then the Python Virtual Machine (PVM) interprets and executes that bytecode. That's why Python is called an interpreted language, even though it performs a compilation step internally.\r\n\r\nThis is the version most interviewers expect.",
