    "answer_hi": "Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Mutable objects create hone ke baad change kiye ja sakte hain, jabki immutable objects creation ke baad change nahi kiye ja sakte. Agar hum kisi immutable object ko modify karte hain, toh Python existing object ko change karne ke bajaye ek naya object create karta hai.\r\n\r\n**Examples:**\r\n\r\n* **Mutable:** `list`, `dict`, `set`\r\n* **Immutable:** `int`, `float`, `str`, `tuple`, `frozenset`\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Mutable data types creation ke baad modify ki ja sakti hain, jabki immutable data types nahi. Common mutable types `list`, `dict`, aur `set` hain, jabki `int`, `str`, aur `tuple` immutable hain.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Mutable = Change kar sakte hain** ✅\r\n* **Immutable = Change nahi kar sakte** ❌",
