    "category": "Data Types",
    "question_hi": "Deep copy aur shallow copy mein kya difference hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Shallow copy ek naya object create karti hai, lekin nested objects original object ke saath shared rehte hain. Deep copy ek completely independent copy create karti hai, jisme saare nested objects bhi included hote hain. Isliye, deep copy mein kiye gaye changes original object ko affect nahi karte.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport copy\r\n\r\na = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]\r\n\r\nb = copy.copy(a)       # Shallow copy\r\nc = copy.deepcopy(a)   # Deep copy\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Shallow copy mein, sirf outer object copy hota hai, jabki nested objects shared rehte hain. Deep copy mein, outer object aur saare nested objects dono copy hote hain, jisse ye completely independent ban jaata hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Shallow Copy = Outer object copy, inner objects shared.**\r\n* **Deep Copy = Sab kuch independently copy hota hai.**",
    "question_en": "What is the difference between deep copy and shallow copy?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> A shallow copy creates a new object, but the nested objects are still shared with the original object. A deep copy creates a completely independent copy, including all nested objects. So, changes made to a deep copy do not affect the original object.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport copy\r\n\r\na = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]\r\n\r\nb = copy.copy(a)       # Shallow copy\r\nc = copy.deepcopy(a)   # Deep copy\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> In a shallow copy, only the outer object is copied, while nested objects are shared. In a deep copy, both the outer object and all nested objects are copied, making it completely independent.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Shallow Copy = Outer object copied, inner objects shared.**\r\n* **Deep Copy = Everything copied independently.**",
