    "question_hi": "String slicing kya hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> String slicing `[start:stop:step]` syntax use karke string ka ek part extract karne ka process hai. `start` index inclusive hota hai, `stop` index exclusive hota hai, aur `step` define karta hai ki har baar kitni positions move karni hain. Agar koi value omit ki jaaye, toh Python default value use karta hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\ntext = \"Hello\"\r\n\r\nprint(text[1:4])   # ell\r\nprint(text[:3])    # Hel\r\nprint(text[::2])   # Hlo\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> String slicing `[start:stop:step]` use karke string ka ek part extract karne ke liye use hoti hai. Ye humein specific characters access karne ya substring create karne deti hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* `start` → kahan se shuru karna hai (included)\r\n* `stop` → kahan khatam karna hai (not included)\r\n* `step` → har baar kitni positions move karni hain",
    "question_en": "What is string slicing?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> String slicing is the process of extracting a part of a string using the syntax `[start:stop:step]`. The `start` index is inclusive, the `stop` index is exclusive, and the `step` defines how many positions to move each time. If any value is omitted, Python uses the default value.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\ntext = \"Hello\"\r\n\r\nprint(text[1:4])   # ell\r\nprint(text[:3])    # Hel\r\nprint(text[::2])   # Hlo\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> String slicing is used to extract a part of a string using `[start:stop:step]`. It allows us to access specific characters or create a substring.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* `start` → where to begin (included)\r\n* `stop` → where to end (not included)\r\n* `step` → how many positions to move each time",
