    "question_hi": "Strings ko efficiently kaise concatenate karte hain?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Python mein multiple strings concatenate karne ka sabse efficient tarika `join()` method use karna hai. Ye baar-baar `+` operator use karne se faster hai kyunki strings immutable hoti hain, aur `join()` final string zyada efficiently create karta hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nwords = [\"Hello\", \"World\"]\r\n\r\nresult = \" \".join(words)\r\n\r\nprint(result)\r\n# Output: Hello World\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Multiple strings ko join karne ke liye, `join()` preferred aur zyada efficient method hai. `+` operator baar-baar use karne se har baar naye string objects create hote hain, jo less efficient hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Kam strings → `+` theek hai.**\r\n* **Zyada strings (especially loops mein) → `''.join()` use karein kyunki ye faster aur zyada efficient hai.**",
    "question_en": "How do you concatenate strings efficiently?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> The most efficient way to concatenate multiple strings in Python is by using the `join()` method. It is faster than using the `+` operator repeatedly because strings are immutable, and `join()` creates the final string more efficiently.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nwords = [\"Hello\", \"World\"]\r\n\r\nresult = \" \".join(words)\r\n\r\nprint(result)\r\n# Output: Hello World\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> For joining multiple strings, `join()` is the preferred and more efficient method. Using the `+` operator repeatedly creates new string objects each time, which is less efficient.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Few strings → `+` is okay.**\r\n* **Many strings (especially in loops) → use `''.join()` because it's faster and more efficient.**",
