    "question_hi": "'is' aur '==' mein kya difference hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> `==` operator do objects ki values compare karta hai ye check karne ke liye ki wo equal hain ya nahi, jabki `is` operator unki identity compare karta hai ye check karne ke liye ki dono variables memory mein same object refer karte hain ya nahi.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\na = [1, 2]\r\nb = [1, 2]\r\n\r\nprint(a == b)   # True  (same values)\r\nprint(a is b)   # False (different objects)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> `==` check karta hai ki values equal hain ya nahi, jabki `is` check karta hai ki do variables memory mein same object refer karte hain ya nahi.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **`==` → Values Compare karo**\r\n* **`is` → Memory/Object Identity Compare karo**",
    "question_en": "What is the difference between 'is' and '=='?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> The `==` operator compares the values of two objects to check if they are equal, while the `is` operator compares their identity to check if both variables refer to the same object in memory.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\na = [1, 2]\r\nb = [1, 2]\r\n\r\nprint(a == b)   # True  (same values)\r\nprint(a is b)   # False (different objects)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> `==` checks whether the values are equal, while `is` checks whether two variables refer to the same object in memory.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **`==` → Compare Values**\r\n* **`is` → Compare Memory/Object Identity**",
