    "question_hi": "Python mein ternary operator kya hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Ternary operator `if-else` statement likhne ka ek one-line tarika hai. Isse ek value choose ki jaati hai agar condition true ho, aur dusri value agar condition false ho.\r\n\r\n**Syntax:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nvalue_if_true if condition else value_if_false\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nage = 18\r\n\r\nstatus = \"Adult\" if age >= 18 else \"Minor\"\r\n\r\nprint(status)\r\n# Output: Adult\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Ternary operator `if-else` statement ka shorthand hai. Isse hum ek conditional expression ko ek hi line mein likh sakte hain, is syntax ka use karke: `value_if_true if condition else value_if_false`.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Normal `if-else` → Multiple lines**\r\n* **Ternary operator → Same logic ek line mein**",
    "question_en": "What is the ternary operator in Python?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> The ternary operator is a one-line way to write an `if-else` statement. It is used to choose one value if a condition is true, and another value if the condition is false.\r\n\r\n**Syntax:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nvalue_if_true if condition else value_if_false\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nage = 18\r\n\r\nstatus = \"Adult\" if age >= 18 else \"Minor\"\r\n\r\nprint(status)\r\n# Output: Adult\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> The ternary operator is a shorthand for an `if-else` statement. It lets us write a conditional expression in a single line using the syntax: `value_if_true if condition else value_if_false`.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Normal `if-else` → Multiple lines**\r\n* **Ternary operator → Same logic in one line**",
