    "category": "Functions",
    "question_hi": "Default arguments kya hain?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Default arguments function parameters hote hain jinki already ek predefined value hoti hai. Agar user function call karte time koi value provide nahi karta, toh Python automatically default value use karta hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef greet(name=\"Guest\"):\r\n    print(\"Hello,\", name)\r\n\r\ngreet()          # Hello, Guest\r\ngreet(\"Vikram\")  # Hello, Vikram\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Default arguments predefined values wale parameters hote hain. Agar function call karte time koi value pass nahi ki jaati, toh Python automatically default value use karta hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Value pass ki → Passed value use hogi.**\r\n* **Value pass nahi ki → Default value use hogi.**",
    "question_en": "What are default arguments?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Default arguments are function parameters that already have a predefined value. If the user does not provide a value while calling the function, Python automatically uses the default value.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef greet(name=\"Guest\"):\r\n    print(\"Hello,\", name)\r\n\r\ngreet()          # Hello, Guest\r\ngreet(\"Vikram\")  # Hello, Vikram\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Default arguments are parameters with predefined values. If no value is passed when calling the function, Python uses the default value automatically.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Value passed → Uses passed value.**\r\n* **No value passed → Uses default value.**",
    "source": "doc",
    "topic": "python",
