    "category": "Functions",
    "question_hi": "Function aur method mein kya difference hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Function code ka ek block hota hai jo independently define kiya jaata hai aur uske naam se directly call kiya ja sakta hai. Method ek function hota hai jo ek class ke andar define kiya jaata hai aur us class ke object ke through call kiya jaata hai. Python mein, methods automatically `self` ko first parameter ke roop mein receive karte hain.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# Function\r\ndef greet():\r\n    print(\"Hello\")\r\n\r\ngreet()\r\n```\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# Method\r\nclass Student:\r\n    def greet(self):\r\n        print(\"Hello\")\r\n\r\ns = Student()\r\ns.greet()\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Function code ka ek independent block hai, jabki method ek class ke andar define hone wala function hai jise object ke through call kiya jaata hai. Methods automatically `self` ko first parameter ke roop mein receive karte hain.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Function → Independent**\r\n* **Method → Class ka part hai aur object ke through call hota hai (`object.method()`)**",
    "question_en": "What is the difference between a function and a method?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> A function is a block of code that is defined independently and can be called directly by its name. A method is a function that is defined inside a class and is called using an object of that class. In Python, methods automatically receive `self` as the first parameter.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# Function\r\ndef greet():\r\n    print(\"Hello\")\r\n\r\ngreet()\r\n```\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# Method\r\nclass Student:\r\n    def greet(self):\r\n        print(\"Hello\")\r\n\r\ns = Student()\r\ns.greet()\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> A function is an independent block of code, while a method is a function defined inside a class and called using an object. Methods automatically receive `self` as the first parameter.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Function → Independent**\r\n* **Method → Belongs to a class and is called through an object (`object.method()`)**",
    "source": "doc",
    "topic": "python",
    "num": "37"
