    "category": "Lists & Tuples",
    "question_hi": "List se elements kaise add ya remove karte hain?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Hum `append()` aur `insert()` jaise methods use karke list mein elements add kar sakte hain. Elements remove karne ke liye, hum `remove()` ya `pop()` use karte hain. `append()` list ke end mein ek item add karta hai, `insert()` ek specific position par item add karta hai, `remove()` ek specific value delete karta hai, aur `pop()` uske index se ek item remove karke usse return karta hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nnumbers = [1, 2, 3]\r\n\r\nnumbers.append(4)      # End mein add\r\nnumbers.insert(1, 10)  # Index 1 par add\r\n\r\nnumbers.remove(2)      # Value 2 remove\r\nnumbers.pop()          # Last item remove\r\n\r\nprint(numbers)\r\n# Output: [1, 10, 3]\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Elements add karne ke liye, hum `append()` ya `insert()` use karte hain. Elements remove karne ke liye, hum `remove()` ya `pop()` use karte hain. `append()` end mein add karta hai, `insert()` ek specific index par add karta hai, `remove()` ek value delete karta hai, aur `pop()` by default index se ya last item remove karta hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **`append()` → End mein add karo**\r\n* **`insert()` → Specific index par add karo**\r\n* **`remove()` → Value se remove karo**\r\n* **`pop()` → Index se (ya default last item) remove karke return karo**",
    "question_en": "How do you add or remove elements from a list?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> We can add elements to a list using methods like `append()` and `insert()`. To remove elements, we use `remove()` or `pop()`. `append()` adds an item at the end of the list, `insert()` adds an item at a specific position, `remove()` deletes a specific value, and `pop()` removes an item by its index and returns it.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nnumbers = [1, 2, 3]\r\n\r\nnumbers.append(4)      # Add at the end\r\nnumbers.insert(1, 10)  # Add at index 1\r\n\r\nnumbers.remove(2)      # Remove value 2\r\nnumbers.pop()          # Remove last item\r\n\r\nprint(numbers)\r\n# Output: [1, 10, 3]\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> To add elements, we use `append()` or `insert()`. To remove elements, we use `remove()` or `pop()`. `append()` adds at the end, `insert()` adds at a specific index, `remove()` deletes a value, and `pop()` removes an item by index or the last item by default.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **`append()` → Add at the end**\r\n* **`insert()` → Add at a specific index**\r\n* **`remove()` → Remove by value**\r\n* **`pop()` → Remove by index (or last item by default) and return it**",
    "source": "doc",
    "topic": "python",
