    "category": "Lists & Tuples",
    "question_hi": "append() aur extend() mein kya difference hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> `append()` aur `extend()` dono list mein elements add karne ke liye use hote hain. Difference ye hai ki `append()` poore object ko ek single element ke roop mein add karta hai, jabki `extend()` ek iterable (jaise list ya tuple) ke har element ko individually existing list mein add karta hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# append()\r\nnumbers = [1, 2]\r\n\r\nnumbers.append([3, 4])\r\n\r\nprint(numbers)\r\n# Output: [1, 2, [3, 4]]\r\n```\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# extend()\r\nnumbers = [1, 2]\r\n\r\nnumbers.extend([3, 4])\r\n\r\nprint(numbers)\r\n# Output: [1, 2, 3, 4]\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> `append()` list ke end mein ek single element add karta hai, jabki `extend()` dusre iterable se saare elements list mein add karta hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **`append()` → Ek item add karta hai (chahe wo list hi ho).**\r\n* **`extend()` → Dusre iterable se har item individually add karta hai.**",
    "question_en": "What is the difference between append() and extend()?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> `append()` and `extend()` are both used to add elements to a list. The difference is that `append()` adds the entire object as a single element, while `extend()` adds each element of an iterable (such as a list or tuple) individually to the existing list.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# append()\r\nnumbers = [1, 2]\r\n\r\nnumbers.append([3, 4])\r\n\r\nprint(numbers)\r\n# Output: [1, 2, [3, 4]]\r\n```\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# extend()\r\nnumbers = [1, 2]\r\n\r\nnumbers.extend([3, 4])\r\n\r\nprint(numbers)\r\n# Output: [1, 2, 3, 4]\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> `append()` adds a single element to the end of the list, while `extend()` adds all elements from another iterable to the list.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **`append()` → Adds one item (even if it's a list).**\r\n* **`extend()` → Adds each item from another iterable individually.**",
