    "category": "Lists & Tuples",
    "question_hi": "List slicing kya hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> List slicing `[start:stop:step]` syntax use karke list ka ek part extract karne ka process hai. Ye selected elements wali ek naya list return karta hai bina original list change kiye.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nnumbers = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]\r\n\r\nprint(numbers[1:4])   # [20, 30, 40]\r\nprint(numbers[:3])    # [10, 20, 30]\r\nprint(numbers[::2])   # [10, 30, 50]\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> List slicing `[start:stop:step]` syntax use karke list ka ek portion extract karne ke liye use hoti hai. Ye original list modify kiye bina ek naya list return karti hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **`start`** → Starting index (included)\r\n* **`stop`** → Ending index (not included)\r\n* **`step`** → Har baar kitni positions move karni hain\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n* `numbers[1:4]` → Index **1** se **3** tak ke elements\r\n* `numbers[::-1]` → List ko reverse karo",
    "question_en": "What is list slicing?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> List slicing is the process of extracting a part of a list using the syntax `[start:stop:step]`. It returns a new list containing the selected elements without changing the original list.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nnumbers = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]\r\n\r\nprint(numbers[1:4])   # [20, 30, 40]\r\nprint(numbers[:3])    # [10, 20, 30]\r\nprint(numbers[::2])   # [10, 30, 50]\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> List slicing is used to extract a portion of a list using the syntax `[start:stop:step]`. It returns a new list without modifying the original list.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **`start`** → Starting index (included)\r\n* **`stop`** → Ending index (not included)\r\n* **`step`** → Number of positions to move each time\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n* `numbers[1:4]` → Elements from index **1** to **3**\r\n* `numbers[::-1]` → Reverse the list",
