    "category": "Lists & Tuples",
    "question_hi": "Tuple ko unpack kaise karte hain?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Tuple unpacking ek tuple ke elements ko ek single statement mein multiple variables mein assign karne ka process hai. Variables ki number tuple elements ki number se match honi chahiye. Hum bache hue elements ko ek list mein collect karne ke liye `*` bhi use kar sakte hain.\r\n\r\n**Example 1 (Basic Unpacking):**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nperson = (\"Vikram\", 22)\r\n\r\nname, age = person\r\n\r\nprint(name)  # Vikram\r\nprint(age)   # 22\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Example 2 (`*` use karke):**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nnumbers = (1, 2, 3, 4, 5)\r\n\r\na, *rest = numbers\r\n\r\nprint(a)     # 1\r\nprint(rest)  # [2, 3, 4, 5]\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Tuple unpacking ka matlab hai tuple elements ko ek statement mein multiple variables mein assign karna. Hum bache hue elements ko list mein collect karne ke liye `*` bhi use kar sakte hain.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Normal unpacking:** `a, b = (10, 20)`\r\n* **Star unpacking:** `a, *rest = (1, 2, 3, 4)` → `rest = [2, 3, 4]`",
    "question_en": "How do you unpack a tuple?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Tuple unpacking is the process of assigning the elements of a tuple to multiple variables in a single statement. The number of variables should match the number of tuple elements. We can also use `*` to collect the remaining elements into a list.\r\n\r\n**Example 1 (Basic Unpacking):**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nperson = (\"Vikram\", 22)\r\n\r\nname, age = person\r\n\r\nprint(name)  # Vikram\r\nprint(age)   # 22\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Example 2 (Using `*`):**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nnumbers = (1, 2, 3, 4, 5)\r\n\r\na, *rest = numbers\r\n\r\nprint(a)     # 1\r\nprint(rest)  # [2, 3, 4, 5]\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Tuple unpacking means assigning tuple elements to multiple variables in one statement. We can also use `*` to collect the remaining elements into a list.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Normal unpacking:** `a, b = (10, 20)`\r\n* **Star unpacking:** `a, *rest = (1, 2, 3, 4)` → `rest = [2, 3, 4]`",
