    "question_hi": "Nested list kya hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Nested list ek aisi list hai jisme apne elements ke roop mein ek ya zyada lists hoti hain. Isse commonly two-dimensional data represent karne ke liye use kiya jaata hai, jaise matrix, table, ya grid. Hum multiple indexes use karke elements access kar sakte hain.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nmatrix = [\r\n    [1, 2],\r\n    [3, 4]\r\n]\r\n\r\nprint(matrix[0][1])   # Output: 2\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Nested list ek list hai jisme dusre lists elements ke roop mein hote hain. Isse commonly two-dimensional data store karne ke liye use kiya jaata hai, aur iske elements multiple indexes use karke access kiye jaate hain.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Normal List:** `[1, 2, 3]`\r\n* **Nested List:** `[[1, 2], [3, 4]]`\r\n* **Element access karo:** `matrix[row][column]`",
