    "category": "Dicts & Sets",
    "question_hi": "Python mein dictionary kya hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Dictionary Python ka ek built-in data type hai jo data ko key-value pairs ke roop mein store karta hai. Isse curly braces `{}` use karke create kiya jaata hai. Har key unique honi chahiye, aur hum unki keys use karke values ko quickly access kar sakte hain. Python 3.7 se, dictionaries elements ka insertion order preserve karti hain.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nstudent = {\r\n    \"name\": \"Vikram\",\r\n    \"age\": 22\r\n}\r\n\r\nprint(student[\"name\"])\r\n# Output: Vikram\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Dictionary key-value pairs ka ek collection hai. Ye values store aur access karne ke liye unique keys use karti hai. Dictionaries `{}` use karke create ki jaati hain aur Python 3.7 aur usse baad insertion order preserve karti hain.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Dictionary = Key : Value**\r\n* **`{}` use karta hai**\r\n* **Keys unique hoti hain**\r\n* **Keys use karke values access karo:** `student[\"name\"]`\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "question_en": "What is a dictionary in Python?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> A dictionary is a built-in data type in Python that stores data as key-value pairs. It is created using curly braces `{}`. Each key must be unique, and we can quickly access values using their keys. From Python 3.7 onwards, dictionaries preserve the insertion order of elements.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nstudent = {\r\n    \"name\": \"Vikram\",\r\n    \"age\": 22\r\n}\r\n\r\nprint(student[\"name\"])\r\n# Output: Vikram\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> A dictionary is a collection of key-value pairs. It uses unique keys to store and access values. Dictionaries are created using `{}` and preserve insertion order in Python 3.7 and later.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Dictionary = Key : Value**\r\n* **Uses `{}`**\r\n* **Keys are unique**\r\n* **Access values using keys:** `student[\"name\"]`\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "source": "doc",
