    "category": "Dicts & Sets",
    "question_hi": "Q.Dictionary internally kaise implement hoti hai?",
    "answer_hi": " A. **Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Python dictionary internally ek hash table use karke implement ki jaati hai. Jab hum ek key-value pair store karte hain, Python key ke liye ek hash value calculate karta hai aur usse quickly find karta hai ki value kahan store hai. Isi wajah se, dictionary operations jaise lookup, insertion, aur deletion bahut fast hoti hain, average time complexity O(1) ke saath.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nstudent = {\r\n    \"name\": \"Vikram\",\r\n    \"age\": 22\r\n}\r\n\r\nprint(student[\"name\"])\r\n# Output: Vikram\r\n```\r\n\r\nYahan, Python `\"name\"` ke hash ka use karke uski value quickly find karta hai.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Dictionary ek hash table use karke implement ki jaati hai. Python key ke hash ka use karke values quickly store aur retrieve karta hai, jisse lookup, insertion, aur deletion bahut fast hoti hain, average time complexity O(1) ke saath.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Dictionary = Hash Table**\r\n* **Key → Hash → Value**\r\n* **Fast operations → Search, insert, aur delete ke liye average `O(1)`**",
    "question_en": "Q.How is a dictionary implemented internally?",
    "answer_en": "A. **Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> A Python dictionary is implemented internally using a hash table. When we store a key-value pair, Python calculates a hash value for the key and uses it to quickly find where the value is stored. Because of this, dictionary operations like lookup, insertion, and deletion are very fast, with an average time complexity of O(1).\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nstudent = {\r\n    \"name\": \"Vikram\",\r\n    \"age\": 22\r\n}\r\n\r\nprint(student[\"name\"])\r\n# Output: Vikram\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere, Python uses the hash of `\"name\"` to quickly find its value.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> A dictionary is implemented using a hash table. Python uses the hash of a key to store and retrieve values quickly, making lookup, insertion, and deletion very fast, with an average time complexity of O(1).\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Dictionary = Hash Table**\r\n* **Key → Hash → Value**\r\n* **Fast operations → Average `O(1)` for search, insert, and delete**",
    "source": "written",
    "topic": "python",
