    "category": "Dicts & Sets",
    "question_hi": "Dictionary aur set mein kya difference hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Dictionary aur set dono built-in Python data types hain, lekin wo data ko differently store karte hain. Dictionary data ko key-value pairs ke roop mein store karti hai, jabki set sirf unique values store karta hai. Dictionaries values access karne ke liye keys use karti hain, jabki sets mainly duplicates remove karne aur union aur intersection jaise set operations perform karne ke liye use hote hain.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# Dictionary\r\nstudent = {\r\n    \"name\": \"Vikram\",\r\n    \"age\": 22\r\n}\r\n\r\nprint(student[\"name\"])\r\n# Output: Vikram\r\n```\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# Set\r\nnumbers = {1, 2, 2, 3, 3}\r\n\r\nprint(numbers)\r\n# Output: {1, 2, 3}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Dictionary data ko key-value pairs ke roop mein store karti hai, jabki set sirf unique values store karta hai. Dictionaries keys ko values se map karne ke liye use hoti hain, aur sets unique elements store karne aur duplicates remove karne ke liye use hote hain.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Dictionary → `key : value` pairs → `{\"name\": \"Vikram\"}`**\r\n* **Set → Sirf unique values → `{1, 2, 3}`**\r\n* **Dictionary `{key: value}` use karti hai**\r\n* **Set `{value1, value2, value3}` use karta hai**",
    "question_en": "What is the difference between a dictionary and a set?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> A dictionary and a set are both built-in Python data types, but they store data differently. A dictionary stores data as key-value pairs, while a set stores only unique values. Dictionaries use keys to access values, whereas sets are mainly used to remove duplicates and perform set operations like union and intersection.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# Dictionary\r\nstudent = {\r\n    \"name\": \"Vikram\",\r\n    \"age\": 22\r\n}\r\n\r\nprint(student[\"name\"])\r\n# Output: Vikram\r\n```\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# Set\r\nnumbers = {1, 2, 2, 3, 3}\r\n\r\nprint(numbers)\r\n# Output: {1, 2, 3}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> A dictionary stores data as key-value pairs, while a set stores only unique values. Dictionaries are used for mapping keys to values, and sets are used to store unique elements and remove duplicates.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Dictionary → `key : value` pairs → `{\"name\": \"Vikram\"}`**\r\n* **Set → Only unique values → `{1, 2, 3}`**\r\n* **Dictionary uses `{key: value}`**\r\n* **Set uses `{value1, value2, value3}`**",
