    "category": "Dicts & Sets",
    "question_hi": "Dictionary ke keys aur values par kaise iterate karte hain?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Hum `keys()`, `values()`, aur `items()` methods use karke dictionary par iterate kar sakte hain. `keys()` sirf keys get karne ke liye use hota hai, `values()` sirf values get karne ke liye use hota hai, aur `items()` keys aur values dono ek saath get karne ke liye use hota hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"o3u4vj\"\r\nstudent = {\r\n    \"name\": \"Vikram\",\r\n    \"age\": 22\r\n}\r\n\r\n# Keys iterate karo\r\nfor key in student.keys():\r\n    print(key)\r\n\r\n# Values iterate karo\r\nfor value in student.values():\r\n    print(value)\r\n\r\n# Key-value pairs iterate karo\r\nfor key, value in student.items():\r\n    print(key, value)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```\r\nname\r\nage\r\nVikram\r\n22\r\nname Vikram\r\nage 22\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Hum `keys()`, `values()`, aur `items()` use karke dictionary par iterate kar sakte hain. `keys()` keys deta hai, `values()` values deta hai, aur `items()` dono key-value pairs deta hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **`dict.keys()` → Sirf keys**\r\n* **`dict.values()` → Sirf values**\r\n* **`dict.items()` → Key + Value saath saath**",
    "question_en": "How do you iterate over a dictionary's keys and values?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> We can iterate over a dictionary using `keys()`, `values()`, and `items()` methods. `keys()` is used to get only keys, `values()` is used to get only values, and `items()` is used to get both keys and values together.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"o3u4vj\"\r\nstudent = {\r\n    \"name\": \"Vikram\",\r\n    \"age\": 22\r\n}\r\n\r\n# Iterate keys\r\nfor key in student.keys():\r\n    print(key)\r\n\r\n# Iterate values\r\nfor value in student.values():\r\n    print(value)\r\n\r\n# Iterate key-value pairs\r\nfor key, value in student.items():\r\n    print(key, value)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```\r\nname\r\nage\r\nVikram\r\n22\r\nname Vikram\r\nage 22\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> We can iterate over a dictionary using `keys()`, `values()`, and `items()`. `keys()` gives keys, `values()` gives values, and `items()` gives both key-value pairs.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **`dict.keys()` → Only keys**\r\n* **`dict.values()` → Only values**\r\n* **`dict.items()` → Key + Value together**",
