    "category": "Dicts & Sets",
    "question_hi": "Dictionary comprehension kya hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Dictionary comprehension ek dictionary ek line mein create karne ka short aur simple tarika hai. Isse hum list comprehension ki tarah expression aur loop use karke key-value pairs generate kar sakte hain.\r\n\r\n**Syntax:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\n{key: value for item in iterable}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"t5q0sk\"\r\nsquares = {x: x**2 for x in range(5)}\r\n\r\nprint(squares)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text\r\n{0: 0, 1: 1, 2: 4, 3: 9, 4: 16}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Dictionary comprehension ek loop aur expression use karke ek line mein dictionary create karne ka tarika hai. Ye key-value pairs create karta hai aur code ko shorter aur cleaner banata hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n**List comprehension:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\n[x*2 for x in range(5)]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Dictionary comprehension:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\n{x: x*2 for x in range(5)}\r\n```\r\n\r\n👉 **Difference: List values deta hai, Dictionary key-value pairs deta hai.**",
    "question_en": "What is a dictionary comprehension?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Dictionary comprehension is a short and simple way to create a dictionary in a single line. It allows us to generate key-value pairs using an expression and a loop, similar to list comprehension.\r\n\r\n**Syntax:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\n{key: value for item in iterable}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"t5q0sk\"\r\nsquares = {x: x**2 for x in range(5)}\r\n\r\nprint(squares)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text\r\n{0: 0, 1: 1, 2: 4, 3: 9, 4: 16}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Dictionary comprehension is a one-line way to create a dictionary using a loop and an expression. It creates key-value pairs and makes code shorter and cleaner.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n**List comprehension:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\n[x*2 for x in range(5)]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Dictionary comprehension:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\n{x: x*2 for x in range(5)}\r\n```\r\n\r\n👉 **Difference: List gives values, Dictionary gives key-value pairs.**",
