    "question_hi": "frozenset kya hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> `frozenset` set ka ek immutable version hai. Ye normal set ki tarah kaam karta hai, lekin ek baar create hone ke baad, hum elements add ya remove nahi kar sakte. Kyunki isse change nahi kiya ja sakta, ye hashable hota hai aur dictionary key ke roop mein use kiya ja sakta hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"m6i6qt\"\r\nnumbers = frozenset([1, 2, 3])\r\n\r\nprint(numbers)\r\n# Output: frozenset({1, 2, 3})\r\n```\r\n\r\n```python id=\"7qg7y8\"\r\n# Modify nahi kar sakte\r\nnumbers.add(4)\r\n# Error: AttributeError\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> `frozenset` ek immutable set hai. Isse creation ke baad modify nahi kiya ja sakta, jisse ye hashable ban jaata hai aur dictionary key ke roop mein use kiya ja sakta hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Set → Mutable → Elements add/remove kar sakte hain**\r\n* **Frozenset → Immutable → Elements change nahi kar sakte**\r\n* **Dono unique values store karte hain**",
    "question_en": "What is a frozenset?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> A `frozenset` is an immutable version of a set. It works like a normal set, but once it is created, we cannot add or remove elements. Since it cannot be changed, it is hashable and can be used as a dictionary key.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"m6i6qt\"\r\nnumbers = frozenset([1, 2, 3])\r\n\r\nprint(numbers)\r\n# Output: frozenset({1, 2, 3})\r\n```\r\n\r\n```python id=\"7qg7y8\"\r\n# Cannot modify\r\nnumbers.add(4)\r\n# Error: AttributeError\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> A `frozenset` is an immutable set. It cannot be modified after creation, which makes it hashable and allows it to be used as a dictionary key.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Set → Mutable → Can add/remove elements**\r\n* **Frozenset → Immutable → Cannot change elements**\r\n* **Both store unique values**",
