    "category": "Dicts & Sets",
    "question_hi": "Do dictionaries ko kaise merge karte hain?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Hum Python mein `update()` method, dictionary unpacking (``), ya Python 3.9 mein introduce kiye gaye merge operator `|` use karke do dictionaries merge kar sakte hain. Agar dono dictionaries mein same key hai, toh dusri dictionary ki value pehli ko overwrite kar deti hai.**\r\n\r\n**Example 1: `update()` use karke**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"1b1z0w\"\r\ndict1 = {\"a\": 1, \"b\": 2}\r\ndict2 = {\"b\": 3, \"c\": 4}\r\n\r\ndict1.update(dict2)\r\n\r\nprint(dict1)\r\n# Output: {'a': 1, 'b': 3, 'c': 4}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Example 2: `|` operator use karke**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"4c8z8z\"\r\ndict3 = dict1 | dict2\r\n\r\nprint(dict3)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Example 3: Unpacking use karke**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"q89z0f\"\r\ndict3 = {**dict1, **dict2}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Hum `update()`, `{dict1, **dict2}`, ya Python 3.9+ mein `|` operator use karke dictionaries merge kar sakte hain. Agar same key dono dictionaries mein exist karti hai, toh dusri dictionary ki value pehli ki jagah le leti hai.**\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **`update()` → Existing dictionary ko modify karta hai**\r\n* **`{**d1, **d2}` → Ek naya dictionary create karta hai**\r\n* **`d1 | d2` → Modern merge operator**\r\n* **Duplicate key → Dusri dictionary jeet-ti hai** ✅",
    "question_en": "How do you merge two dictionaries?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> We can merge two dictionaries in Python using the `update()` method, dictionary unpacking (``), or the merge operator `|` introduced in Python 3.9. If both dictionaries have the same key, the value from the second dictionary overwrites the first one.**\r\n\r\n**Example 1: Using `update()`**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"1b1z0w\"\r\ndict1 = {\"a\": 1, \"b\": 2}\r\ndict2 = {\"b\": 3, \"c\": 4}\r\n\r\ndict1.update(dict2)\r\n\r\nprint(dict1)\r\n# Output: {'a': 1, 'b': 3, 'c': 4}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Example 2: Using `|` operator**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"4c8z8z\"\r\ndict3 = dict1 | dict2\r\n\r\nprint(dict3)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Example 3: Using unpacking**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"q89z0f\"\r\ndict3 = {**dict1, **dict2}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> We can merge dictionaries using `update()`, `{dict1, **dict2}`, or the `|` operator in Python 3.9+. If the same key exists in both dictionaries, the second dictionary's value replaces the first one.**\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **`update()` → Modifies existing dictionary**\r\n* **`{**d1, **d2}` → Creates a new dictionary**\r\n* **`d1 | d2` → Modern merge operator**\r\n* **Duplicate key → Second dictionary wins** ✅",
    "source": "doc",
    "topic": "python",
