    "category": "OOP",
    "question_hi": "Class aur object kya hain?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Class ek blueprint ya template hai jo objects create karne ke liye use hota hai. Ye properties (attributes) aur behaviors (methods) define karta hai jo objects mein honge. Object ek class ka instance hota hai jisme apna data hota hai aur wo class mein defined methods use kar sakta hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"u4j9hz\"\r\nclass Student:\r\n    def __init__(self, name):\r\n        self.name = name\r\n\r\n    def display(self):\r\n        print(self.name)\r\n\r\n# Object creation\r\nstudent1 = Student(\"Vikram\")\r\n\r\nstudent1.display()\r\n# Output: Vikram\r\n```\r\n\r\nYahan:\r\n\r\n* **Class → Student (Blueprint)**\r\n* **Object → student1 (Student class ka real instance)**\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Class ek blueprint hai jo attributes aur methods define karta hai, jabki object us class ka ek instance hai. Objects class dwara defined properties aur behaviors use karte hain.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Class = Blueprint (jaise ek house design)**\r\n* **Object = Blueprint se create hui actual cheez (actual house)**",
    "question_en": "What is a class and an object?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> A class is a blueprint or template used to create objects. It defines the properties (attributes) and behaviors (methods) that objects will have. An object is an instance of a class that contains its own data and can use the methods defined in the class.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"u4j9hz\"\r\nclass Student:\r\n    def __init__(self, name):\r\n        self.name = name\r\n\r\n    def display(self):\r\n        print(self.name)\r\n\r\n# Object creation\r\nstudent1 = Student(\"Vikram\")\r\n\r\nstudent1.display()\r\n# Output: Vikram\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere:\r\n\r\n* **Class → Student (Blueprint)**\r\n* **Object → student1 (Real instance of Student class)**\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> A class is a blueprint that defines attributes and methods, while an object is an instance of that class. Objects use the properties and behaviors defined by the class.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Class = Blueprint (like a house design)**\r\n* **Object = Actual thing created from blueprint (actual house)**",
