    "category": "OOP",
    "question_hi": "__init__ kis liye use hota hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> `__init__` Python mein ek constructor method hai. Jab bhi ek naya object create hota hai ye automatically call hota hai. Isse mainly object ke attributes initialize karne aur unki initial values set karne ke liye use kiya jaata hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"l0g3fs\"\r\nclass Student:\r\n    def __init__(self, name, age):\r\n        self.name = name\r\n        self.age = age\r\n\r\nstudent1 = Student(\"Vikram\", 22)\r\n\r\nprint(student1.name)\r\n# Output: Vikram\r\n```\r\n\r\nYahan, `__init__` object create hote hi `name` aur `age` ki initial values set karta hai.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> `__init__` ek constructor method hai jo object create hote hi automatically run hota hai. Isse object attributes ko initial values ke saath initialize karne ke liye use kiya jaata hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Object create hua → `__init__` automatically run hota hai**\r\n* **Purpose → Object data initialize karna**\r\n* **`self` → Current object ko refer karta hai**",
    "question_en": "What is __init__ used for?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> `__init__` is a constructor method in Python. It is automatically called when a new object is created. It is mainly used to initialize the object's attributes and set their initial values.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"l0g3fs\"\r\nclass Student:\r\n    def __init__(self, name, age):\r\n        self.name = name\r\n        self.age = age\r\n\r\nstudent1 = Student(\"Vikram\", 22)\r\n\r\nprint(student1.name)\r\n# Output: Vikram\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere, `__init__` sets the initial values of `name` and `age` when the object is created.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> `__init__` is a constructor method that runs automatically when an object is created. It is used to initialize object attributes with initial values.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Object created → `__init__` runs automatically**\r\n* **Purpose → Initialize object data**\r\n* **`self` → Refers to the current object**",
    "source": "doc",
