    "category": "OOP",
    "question_hi": "__init__ aur __new__ mein kya difference hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> `__new__` aur `__init__` dono object creation ke dauraan use hone wale special methods hain. `__new__` naya object create aur return karne ke liye responsible hai, aur ye pehle run hota hai. Object create hone ke baad, `__init__` object ke attributes initialize karne ke liye call hota hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"w2z0qn\"\r\nclass Student:\r\n    def __new__(cls):\r\n        print(\"Creating object\")\r\n        return super().__new__(cls)\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self):\r\n        print(\"Initializing object\")\r\n\r\nstudent1 = Student()\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```\r\nCreating object\r\nInitializing object\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> `__new__` object create karta hai aur pehle run hota hai, jabki `__init__` object ka data initialize karta hai aur `__new__` ke baad run hota hai. Most cases mein, hum `__init__` use karte hain, aur `__new__` special cases jaise object creation customize karne ke liye use hota hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **`__new__` → Object create karta hai** 🏗️\r\n* **`__init__` → Object data initialize karta hai** ⚙️\r\n* **Order:** `__new__` → `__init__` ✅",
    "question_en": "What is the difference between __init__ and __new__?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> `__new__` and `__init__` both are special methods used during object creation. `__new__` is responsible for creating and returning a new object, and it runs first. After the object is created, `__init__` is called to initialize the object's attributes.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"w2z0qn\"\r\nclass Student:\r\n    def __new__(cls):\r\n        print(\"Creating object\")\r\n        return super().__new__(cls)\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self):\r\n        print(\"Initializing object\")\r\n\r\nstudent1 = Student()\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```\r\nCreating object\r\nInitializing object\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> `__new__` creates the object and runs first, while `__init__` initializes the object's data and runs after `__new__`. In most cases, we use `__init__`, and `__new__` is used for special cases like customizing object creation.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **`__new__` → Creates object 🏗️**\r\n* **`__init__` → Initializes object data ⚙️**\r\n* **Order:** `__new__` → `__init__` ✅",
