    "category": "OOP",
    "question_hi": "Inheritance kya hai? Example dein.",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Inheritance ek OOP feature hai jo ek child class ko parent class ki properties aur methods use karne deta hai. Ye code reuse mein madad karta hai aur code duplication kam karta hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"0q3v7m\"\r\nclass Animal:\r\n    def sound(self):\r\n        print(\"Animal makes a sound\")\r\n\r\nclass Dog(Animal):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\ndog = Dog()\r\ndog.sound()\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text\r\nAnimal makes a sound\r\n```\r\n\r\nYahan:\r\n\r\n* **Animal → Parent class**\r\n* **Dog → Child class**\r\n* **Dog `sound()` method ko Animal se inherit karta hai**\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Inheritance ek class ko dusri class ke attributes aur methods inherit karne deta hai. Existing class ko parent class kaha jaata hai, aur naye class ko child class kaha jaata hai. Isse mainly code reusability ke liye use kiya jaata hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Parent class → Features deta hai**\r\n* **Child class → Inherited features use karta hai**\r\n* **Benefit → Code reuse** ✅",
    "question_en": "What is inheritance? Give an example.",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Inheritance is an OOP feature that allows a child class to use the properties and methods of a parent class. It helps in code reuse and reduces code duplication.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"0q3v7m\"\r\nclass Animal:\r\n    def sound(self):\r\n        print(\"Animal makes a sound\")\r\n\r\nclass Dog(Animal):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\ndog = Dog()\r\ndog.sound()\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text\r\nAnimal makes a sound\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere:\r\n\r\n* **Animal → Parent class**\r\n* **Dog → Child class**\r\n* **Dog inherits the `sound()` method from Animal**\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Inheritance allows one class to inherit the attributes and methods of another class. The existing class is called the parent class, and the new class is called the child class. It is mainly used for code reusability.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Parent class → Gives features**\r\n* **Child class → Uses inherited features**\r\n* **Benefit → Code reuse** ✅",
