    "category": "OOP",
    "question_hi": "Method overriding kya hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Method overriding OOP ki ek feature hai jisme ek child class kisi method ka apna implementation provide karta hai jo already parent class mein defined hai. Jab hum us method ko child class object use karke call karte hain, toh parent class method ke bajaye child class method execute hota hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"k3n2ps\"\r\nclass Animal:\r\n    def sound(self):\r\n        print(\"Animal makes a sound\")\r\n\r\nclass Dog(Animal):\r\n    def sound(self):\r\n        print(\"Dog barks\")\r\n\r\ndog = Dog()\r\ndog.sound()\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text\r\nDog barks\r\n```\r\n\r\nYahan:\r\n\r\n* `Animal` → Parent class\r\n* `Dog` → Child class\r\n* `sound()` method `Dog` mein override kiya gaya hai\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Method overriding tab hoti hai jab child class parent class method ke same naam se ek method define karta hai. Child class method, child object use karke call karne par parent method ko replace kar deta hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Same method name**\r\n* **Parent → Old implementation**\r\n* **Child → New implementation**\r\n* **Child method ko priority milti hai** ✅",
    "question_en": "What is method overriding?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Method overriding is a feature of OOP where a child class provides its own implementation of a method that is already defined in the parent class. When we call that method using the child class object, the child class method is executed instead of the parent class method.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"k3n2ps\"\r\nclass Animal:\r\n    def sound(self):\r\n        print(\"Animal makes a sound\")\r\n\r\nclass Dog(Animal):\r\n    def sound(self):\r\n        print(\"Dog barks\")\r\n\r\ndog = Dog()\r\ndog.sound()\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text\r\nDog barks\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere:\r\n\r\n* `Animal` → Parent class\r\n* `Dog` → Child class\r\n* `sound()` method is overridden in `Dog`\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Method overriding happens when a child class defines a method with the same name as the parent class method. The child class method replaces the parent method when called using the child object.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Same method name**\r\n* **Parent → Old implementation**\r\n* **Child → New implementation**\r\n* **Child method gets priority** ✅",
    "source": "doc",
