    "category": "OOP",
    "question_hi": "Encapsulation kya hai, aur ye Python mein kaise achieve hoti hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Encapsulation ek OOP concept hai jiska matlab hai data (attributes) aur methods ko ek class ke andar saath mein wrap karna aur data tak access control karna. Ye object ke internal details ko protect karne mein madad karta hai aur unwanted changes prevent karta hai. Python mein, encapsulation `_single underscore` aur `__double underscore` jaise naming conventions use karke achieve ki jaati hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"r5h7x2\"\r\nclass BankAccount:\r\n    def __init__(self, balance):\r\n        self.__balance = balance   # Private attribute\r\n\r\n    def get_balance(self):\r\n        return self.__balance\r\n\r\naccount = BankAccount(5000)\r\n\r\nprint(account.get_balance())\r\n# Output: 5000\r\n```\r\n\r\nYahan:\r\n\r\n* `_balance` → Protected (convention ke through)\r\n* `__balance` → Private (name mangling)\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Encapsulation ka matlab hai internal data hide karna aur usme access control karna. Python mein, ye protected attributes ke liye `_` aur private attributes ke liye `__` use karke achieve ki jaati hai. Ye data ko safe aur maintainable rakhne mein madad karta hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Encapsulation = Data hiding + Controlled access**\r\n* **`_name` → Protected**\r\n* **`__name` → Private-like** ✅",
    "question_en": "What is encapsulation, and how is it achieved in Python?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Encapsulation is an OOP concept that means wrapping data (attributes) and methods together inside a class and controlling access to the data. It helps protect the internal details of an object and prevents unwanted changes. In Python, encapsulation is achieved using naming conventions like `_single underscore` and `__double underscore`.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"r5h7x2\"\r\nclass BankAccount:\r\n    def __init__(self, balance):\r\n        self.__balance = balance   # Private attribute\r\n\r\n    def get_balance(self):\r\n        return self.__balance\r\n\r\naccount = BankAccount(5000)\r\n\r\nprint(account.get_balance())\r\n# Output: 5000\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere:\r\n\r\n* `_balance` → Protected (by convention)\r\n* `__balance` → Private (name mangling)\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Encapsulation means hiding internal data and controlling access to it. In Python, it is achieved using `_` for protected attributes and `__` for private attributes. It helps keep data safe and maintainable.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Encapsulation = Data hiding + Controlled access**\r\n* **`_name` → Protected**\r\n* **`__name` → Private-like** ✅",
    "source": "doc",
    "topic": "python",
    "num": "70"
