    "category": "OOP",
    "question_hi": "Polymorphism kya hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Polymorphism ek OOP concept hai jisme same method ya operation object ke basis par different behave kar sakta hai. Ye different classes ko same method name ke saath different implementations use karne deta hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"8jv4qa\"\r\nclass Dog:\r\n    def sound(self):\r\n        print(\"Bark\")\r\n\r\nclass Cat:\r\n    def sound(self):\r\n        print(\"Meow\")\r\n\r\ndog = Dog()\r\ncat = Cat()\r\n\r\ndog.sound()\r\ncat.sound()\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text id=\"q7d5m3\"\r\nBark\r\nMeow\r\n```\r\n\r\nYahan, same method `sound()` different objects ke liye differently behave karta hai.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Polymorphism ka matlab hai \"many forms\". Ye same method ya function ko call karne wale object ke basis par different actions perform karne deta hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Poly → Many**\r\n* **Morph → Forms**\r\n* **Same method name → Different behavior** ✅\r\n\r\n**Real-life example:**\r\n\r\n* `len(\"Python\")` → characters count karta hai\r\n* `len([1,2,3])` → list items count karta hai\r\n  Same function, different behavior.",
    "question_en": "What is polymorphism?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Polymorphism is an OOP concept where the same method or operation can behave differently depending on the object. It allows different classes to use the same method name with different implementations.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"8jv4qa\"\r\nclass Dog:\r\n    def sound(self):\r\n        print(\"Bark\")\r\n\r\nclass Cat:\r\n    def sound(self):\r\n        print(\"Meow\")\r\n\r\ndog = Dog()\r\ncat = Cat()\r\n\r\ndog.sound()\r\ncat.sound()\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text id=\"q7d5m3\"\r\nBark\r\nMeow\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere, the same method `sound()` behaves differently for different objects.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Polymorphism means \"many forms\". It allows the same method or function to perform different actions depending on the object that calls it.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Poly → Many**\r\n* **Morph → Forms**\r\n* **Same method name → Different behavior** ✅\r\n\r\n**Real-life example:**\r\n\r\n* `len(\"Python\")` → counts characters\r\n* `len([1,2,3])` → counts list items\r\n  Same function, different behavior.",
