    "category": "OOP",
    "question_hi": "Superclass aur subclass mein kya difference hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Superclass wo parent class hai jisse dusri class properties aur methods inherit karti hai. Subclass wo child class hai jo superclass se un properties aur methods ko inherit karti hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"q7p8mz\"\r\nclass Animal:        # Superclass\r\n    def sound(self):\r\n        print(\"Animal sound\")\r\n\r\nclass Dog(Animal):   # Subclass\r\n    pass\r\n\r\ndog = Dog()\r\ndog.sound()\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text id=\"3m6y0s\"\r\nAnimal sound\r\n```\r\n\r\nYahan:\r\n\r\n* **Animal → Superclass (Parent/Base class)**\r\n* **Dog → Subclass (Child/Derived class)**\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Superclass wo class hai jo inheritance ke liye properties aur methods provide karti hai, jabki subclass wo class hai jo un properties aur methods ko receive aur use karti hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Super class = Features deti hai**\r\n* **Sub class = Features leti hai**\r\n* **Parent → Child relationship** ✅",
    "question_en": "What is the difference between a superclass and a subclass?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> A superclass is the parent class from which another class inherits properties and methods. A subclass is the child class that inherits those properties and methods from the superclass.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"q7p8mz\"\r\nclass Animal:        # Superclass\r\n    def sound(self):\r\n        print(\"Animal sound\")\r\n\r\nclass Dog(Animal):   # Subclass\r\n    pass\r\n\r\ndog = Dog()\r\ndog.sound()\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text id=\"3m6y0s\"\r\nAnimal sound\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere:\r\n\r\n* **Animal → Superclass (Parent/Base class)**\r\n* **Dog → Subclass (Child/Derived class)**\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> A superclass is the class that provides properties and methods for inheritance, while a subclass is the class that receives and uses those properties and methods.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Super class = Gives features**\r\n* **Sub class = Gets features**\r\n* **Parent → Child relationship** ✅",
    "source": "doc",
    "topic": "python",
