    "category": "Exceptions",
    "question_hi": "Exception handling kya hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Exception handling ek program mein runtime errors ko bina execution roke handle karne ka tarika hai. Python errors ko gracefully catch aur manage karne ke liye `try`, `except`, `else`, aur `finally` blocks use karta hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"2n6p9v\"\r\ntry:\r\n    a = 10\r\n    b = 0\r\n    print(a / b)\r\n\r\nexcept ZeroDivisionError:\r\n    print(\"Cannot divide by zero\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text id=\"6v5w8k\"\r\nCannot divide by zero\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Blocks:**\r\n\r\n* **try** → Us code ko contain karta hai jisse error ho sakta hai.\r\n* **except** → Error handle karta hai.\r\n* **else** → Koi error na aane par run hota hai.\r\n* **finally** → Hamesha run hota hai, chahe error aaye ya nahi.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Exception handling ka use program execution ke dauraan errors handle karne aur program ko crash hone se bachane ke liye kiya jaata hai. Python mein, hum exceptions catch aur handle karne ke liye `try` aur `except` blocks use karte hain.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **try → Risky code try karo**\r\n* **except → Error handle karo**\r\n* **else → Agar successful ho**\r\n* **finally → Hamesha execute karo** ✅",
    "question_en": "What is exception handling?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Exception handling is a way to handle runtime errors in a program without stopping its execution. Python uses `try`, `except`, `else`, and `finally` blocks to catch and manage errors gracefully.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"2n6p9v\"\r\ntry:\r\n    a = 10\r\n    b = 0\r\n    print(a / b)\r\n\r\nexcept ZeroDivisionError:\r\n    print(\"Cannot divide by zero\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text id=\"6v5w8k\"\r\nCannot divide by zero\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Blocks:**\r\n\r\n* **try** → Contains code that may cause an error.\r\n* **except** → Handles the error.\r\n* **else** → Runs if no error occurs.\r\n* **finally** → Always runs, whether an error occurs or not.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Exception handling is used to handle errors during program execution and prevent the program from crashing. In Python, we use `try` and `except` blocks to catch and handle exceptions.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **try → Try risky code**\r\n* **except → Handle error**\r\n* **else → If successful**\r\n* **finally → Always execute** ✅",
    "source": "doc",
    "topic": "python",
    "num": "77"
