    "category": "Exceptions",
    "question_hi": "Exception aur BaseException mein kya difference hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> `BaseException` Python mein saare exceptions ki root class hai. Isme `KeyboardInterrupt` aur `SystemExit` jaise system-level exceptions shamil hain. `Exception`, `BaseException` ki ek subclass hai aur most common errors ke liye base class hai jo hum programs mein handle karte hain.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"m4q7tz\"\r\ntry:\r\n    x = 10 / 0\r\n\r\nexcept Exception:\r\n    print(\"An error occurred\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text id=\"9kq1hf\"\r\nAn error occurred\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Difference:**\r\n\r\n| BaseException                   | Exception                                                     |\r\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\r\n| Saare exceptions ki root class    | Normal errors ke liye base class                                  |\r\n| System exit exceptions include karta hai | ValueError, TypeError, ZeroDivisionError jaise errors include karta hai |\r\n| Usually directly catch nahi kiya jaata     | try-except blocks mein commonly use hota hai                            |\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> `BaseException` Python mein saare exceptions ki top-level parent class hai. `Exception` isse derive hoti hai aur normal runtime errors handle karne ke liye use hoti hai. Most cases mein, hum `Exception` ko catch karte hain, `BaseException` ko nahi.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **BaseException → Sab kuch**\r\n* **Exception → Normal program errors** ✅",
    "question_en": "What is the difference between Exception and BaseException?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> `BaseException` is the root class of all exceptions in Python. It includes system-level exceptions like `KeyboardInterrupt` and `SystemExit`. `Exception` is a subclass of `BaseException` and is the base class for most common errors that we handle in programs.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"m4q7tz\"\r\ntry:\r\n    x = 10 / 0\r\n\r\nexcept Exception:\r\n    print(\"An error occurred\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text id=\"9kq1hf\"\r\nAn error occurred\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Difference:**\r\n\r\n| BaseException                   | Exception                                                     |\r\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\r\n| Root class of all exceptions    | Base class for normal errors                                  |\r\n| Includes system exit exceptions | Includes errors like ValueError, TypeError, ZeroDivisionError |\r\n| Usually not caught directly     | Commonly used in try-except blocks                            |\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> `BaseException` is the top-level parent class of all exceptions in Python. `Exception` is derived from it and is used for handling normal runtime errors. In most cases, we catch `Exception`, not `BaseException`.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **BaseException → Everything**\r\n* **Exception → Normal program errors** ✅",
    "source": "doc",
    "topic": "python",
    "num": "78"
