    "category": "Exceptions",
    "question_hi": "finally block ka purpose kya hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> `finally` block ka use us code ko execute karne ke liye kiya jaata hai jo hamesha run hona chahiye, chahe exception aaye ya nahi. Isse mainly cleanup tasks jaise files close karna, database connections close karna, ya resources release karne ke liye use kiya jaata hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"8m4xq1\"\r\ntry:\r\n    file = open(\"data.txt\", \"r\")\r\n    print(file.read())\r\n\r\nexcept FileNotFoundError:\r\n    print(\"File not found\")\r\n\r\nfinally:\r\n    print(\"Closing resources\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text id=\"2j6k9p\"\r\nClosing resources\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> `finally` block `try` aur `except` ke baad hamesha execute hota hai. Isse cleanup operations ke liye use kiya jaata hai jo error aaye ya na aaye, hamesha perform hone chahiye.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **try → Risky code run karo**\r\n* **except → Error handle karo**\r\n* **finally → Cleanup code hamesha execute karo** ✅",
    "question_en": "What is the purpose of the finally block?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> The `finally` block is used to execute code that should always run, whether an exception occurs or not. It is mainly used for cleanup tasks like closing files, closing database connections, or releasing resources.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"8m4xq1\"\r\ntry:\r\n    file = open(\"data.txt\", \"r\")\r\n    print(file.read())\r\n\r\nexcept FileNotFoundError:\r\n    print(\"File not found\")\r\n\r\nfinally:\r\n    print(\"Closing resources\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Output:**\r\n\r\n```text id=\"2j6k9p\"\r\nClosing resources\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> The `finally` block always executes after `try` and `except`. It is used for cleanup operations that must be performed regardless of whether an error occurs or not.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **try → Run risky code**\r\n* **except → Handle error**\r\n* **finally → Always execute cleanup code** ✅",
    "source": "doc",
    "topic": "python",
    "num": "79"
