    "category": "Exceptions",
    "question_hi": "raise aur assert mein kya difference hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> `raise` aur `assert` dono errors generate karne ke liye use hote hain, lekin inka use different purposes ke liye hota hai. `raise` ka use manually ek exception create aur throw karne ke liye kiya jaata hai, jabki `assert` ka use ye check karne ke liye kiya jaata hai ki koi condition true hai ya nahi aur agar condition false ho toh `AssertionError` raise karta hai.\r\n\r\n**`raise` ka example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"8k3p1m\"\r\nage = -1\r\n\r\nif age < 0:\r\n    raise ValueError(\"Age cannot be negative\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nYahan, hum manually ek error create karte hain.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**`assert` ka example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"9v4q2s\"\r\nage = 18\r\n\r\nassert age >= 18, \"Age must be 18 or above\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nAgar condition false ho, toh Python `AssertionError` raise karta hai.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> `raise` ka use manually exception trigger karne ke liye kiya jaata hai jab hum chahte hain. `assert` ka use debugging ke dauraan ek condition test karne ke liye kiya jaata hai aur agar condition false ho toh automatically `AssertionError` raise karta hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **raise → \"Main ek error create karna chahta hoon\"**\r\n* **assert → \"Mujhe expect hai ki ye condition true ho\"**\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n* `raise ValueError` → User input galat hai\r\n* `assert x > 0` → Developer code logic check karta hai ✅",
    "question_en": "What is the difference between raise and assert?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> `raise` and `assert` are both used to generate errors, but they are used for different purposes. `raise` is used to manually create and throw an exception, while `assert` is used to check whether a condition is true and raises an `AssertionError` if the condition is false.\r\n\r\n**Example of `raise`:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"8k3p1m\"\r\nage = -1\r\n\r\nif age < 0:\r\n    raise ValueError(\"Age cannot be negative\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere, we manually create an error.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Example of `assert`:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"9v4q2s\"\r\nage = 18\r\n\r\nassert age >= 18, \"Age must be 18 or above\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf the condition is false, Python raises `AssertionError`.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> `raise` is used to manually trigger an exception when we want. `assert` is used to test a condition during debugging and automatically raises `AssertionError` if the condition is false.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **raise → \"I want to create an error\"**\r\n* **assert → \"I expect this condition to be true\"**\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n* `raise ValueError` → User input is wrong\r\n* `assert x > 0` → Developer checks code logic ✅",
