    "category": "Exceptions",
    "question_hi": "Kya hum ek except block mein multiple exceptions catch kar sakte hain?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Haan, hum multiple exception types ko ek tuple ke roop mein pass karke single `except` block mein multiple exceptions catch kar sakte hain. Ye tab useful hota hai jab hum different errors ko same tarike se handle karna chahte hain.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"n5j8qa\"\r\ntry:\r\n    value = int(\"abc\")\r\n    result = 10 / 0\r\n\r\nexcept (ValueError, ZeroDivisionError):\r\n    print(\"An error occurred\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nYahan, same `except` block handle karta hai:\r\n\r\n* `ValueError` → Invalid conversion\r\n* `ZeroDivisionError` → Zero se division\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Haan, Python exception types ka ek tuple use karke ek `except` block mein multiple exceptions handle karne deta hai. Isse un errors ke liye separate blocks likhne se bacha jaata hai jinhe same handling chahiye hoti hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nexcept (Error1, Error2):\r\n    # dono errors handle karo\r\n```\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nexcept (ValueError, TypeError):\r\n    print(\"Invalid input\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n✅ Ek block → Multiple errors handle.",
    "question_en": "Can you catch multiple exceptions in one except block?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Yes, we can catch multiple exceptions in a single `except` block by passing multiple exception types as a tuple. This is useful when we want to handle different errors in the same way.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"n5j8qa\"\r\ntry:\r\n    value = int(\"abc\")\r\n    result = 10 / 0\r\n\r\nexcept (ValueError, ZeroDivisionError):\r\n    print(\"An error occurred\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere, the same `except` block handles:\r\n\r\n* `ValueError` → Invalid conversion\r\n* `ZeroDivisionError` → Division by zero\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Yes, Python allows handling multiple exceptions in one `except` block by using a tuple of exception types. It helps avoid writing separate blocks for errors that need the same handling.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nexcept (Error1, Error2):\r\n    # handle both errors\r\n```\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nexcept (ValueError, TypeError):\r\n    print(\"Invalid input\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n✅ One block → Multiple errors handle.",
