    "category": "File Handling",
    "question_hi": "File ko line by line kaise read karte hain?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Hum file object par iterate karne ke liye `for` loop use karke file ko line by line read kar sakte hain. Ye ek time par ek line read karta hai aur memory efficient hota hai, especially large files ke liye.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"p6k3vw\"\r\nwith open(\"data.txt\", \"r\") as file:\r\n    for line in file:\r\n        print(line)\r\n```\r\n\r\nYahan:\r\n\r\n* `for` loop har line ko ek-ek karke read karta hai.\r\n* `with` ki wajah se file automatically close ho jaati hai.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Hum file object par `for` loop use karke loop chala kar file ko line by line read kar sakte hain. Ye ek time par ek line read karta hai, jo large files ke liye memory save karta hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfor line in file:\r\n    print(line)\r\n```\r\n\r\n✅ **Ek loop → Ek time par ek line**",
    "question_en": "How do you read a file line by line?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> We can read a file line by line by using a `for` loop to iterate over the file object. This reads one line at a time and is memory efficient, especially for large files.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"p6k3vw\"\r\nwith open(\"data.txt\", \"r\") as file:\r\n    for line in file:\r\n        print(line)\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere:\r\n\r\n* The `for` loop reads each line one by one.\r\n* The file is automatically closed because of `with`.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> We can read a file line by line by looping through the file object using a `for` loop. It reads one line at a time, which saves memory for large files.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfor line in file:\r\n    print(line)\r\n```\r\n\r\n✅ **One loop → One line at a time**",
