    "question_hi": "Python mein file mein kaise likhte hain?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Python mein, hum data ko file mein likhne ke liye usse write mode (`w`) ya append mode (`a`) mein open karke `write()` method use karte hain. `write()` method ek string ko file mein likhta hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"k9p4vx\"\r\nwith open(\"data.txt\", \"w\") as file:\r\n    file.write(\"Hello Python\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nYahan:\r\n\r\n* `\"w\"` → File ko writing ke liye open karta hai (old content replace ho jaata hai).\r\n* `\"a\"` → File ko appending ke liye open karta hai (end mein data add karta hai).\r\n* `write()` → File mein data likhta hai.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Hum file ko `w` ya `a` mode mein open karke aur `write()` method use karke file mein likh sakte hain. `w` existing content replace karta hai, jabki `a` end mein naya content add karta hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"r7s2nf\"\r\n# Write mode\r\nwith open(\"file.txt\", \"w\") as f:\r\n    f.write(\"Hello\")\r\n\r\n# Append mode\r\nwith open(\"file.txt\", \"a\") as f:\r\n    f.write(\" Python\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n✅ **`w` = Write/Replace**\r\n✅ **`a` = End mein add karo**",
    "question_en": "How do you write to a file in Python?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> In Python, we can write data to a file by opening it in write mode (`w`) or append mode (`a`) and using the `write()` method. The `write()` method writes a string into the file.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"k9p4vx\"\r\nwith open(\"data.txt\", \"w\") as file:\r\n    file.write(\"Hello Python\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere:\r\n\r\n* `\"w\"` → Opens the file for writing (old content is replaced).\r\n* `\"a\"` → Opens the file for appending (adds data at the end).\r\n* `write()` → Writes data into the file.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> We can write to a file by opening it using `w` or `a` mode and using the `write()` method. `w` replaces existing content, while `a` adds new content at the end.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n```python id=\"r7s2nf\"\r\n# Write mode\r\nwith open(\"file.txt\", \"w\") as f:\r\n    f.write(\"Hello\")\r\n\r\n# Append mode\r\nwith open(\"file.txt\", \"a\") as f:\r\n    f.write(\" Python\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n✅ **`w` = Write/Replace**\r\n✅ **`a` = Add at end**",
