    "category": "Modules",
    "question_hi": "Module aur package mein kya difference hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Module ek single Python file hai jisme functions, classes, ya variables jaisa reusable code hota hai. Package multiple modules ka ek collection hai jo bade projects manage karne ke liye ek folder ke andar organize kiya jaata hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n### **Module:**\r\n\r\n`math_utils.py`\r\n\r\n```python id=\"p8m3vd\"\r\ndef add(a, b):\r\n    return a + b\r\n```\r\n\r\nYahan, `math_utils.py` ek module hai.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Package:**\r\n\r\n```\r\nmy_package/\r\n    __init__.py\r\n    math_utils.py\r\n    string_utils.py\r\n```\r\n\r\nYahan, `my_package` ek package hai jisme multiple modules hain.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Module ek single `.py` file hai jisme reusable code hota hai, jabki package multiple modules wala ek folder hai. Packages large Python applications ko organize karne mein madad karte hain.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Module → Ek Python file (`.py`)**\r\n* **Package → Modules ka collection (folder)** ✅",
    "question_en": "What is the difference between a module and a package?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> A module is a single Python file that contains reusable code like functions, classes, or variables. A package is a collection of multiple modules organized inside a folder to manage larger projects.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n### **Module:**\r\n\r\n`math_utils.py`\r\n\r\n```python id=\"p8m3vd\"\r\ndef add(a, b):\r\n    return a + b\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere, `math_utils.py` is a module.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Package:**\r\n\r\n```\r\nmy_package/\r\n    __init__.py\r\n    math_utils.py\r\n    string_utils.py\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere, `my_package` is a package containing multiple modules.\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> A module is a single `.py` file containing reusable code, while a package is a folder containing multiple modules. Packages help organize large Python applications.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Module → One Python file (`.py`)**\r\n* **Package → Collection of modules (folder)** ✅",
