    "category": "Modules",
    "question_hi": "pip kya hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Pip Python ka package manager hai jo external libraries ya packages install, update, aur remove karne ke liye use hota hai. Ye developers ko Python Package Index (PyPI) se apne Python projects mein extra functionality add karne mein madad karta hai.\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npip install requests\r\n```\r\n\r\nYe command `requests` library install karta hai.\r\n\r\nOther commands:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npip uninstall requests\r\n```\r\n\r\n→ Ek package remove karta hai\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npip install --upgrade requests\r\n```\r\n\r\n→ Ek package update karta hai\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Pip ek tool hai jo Python packages manage karne ke liye use hota hai. Ye humein third-party libraries install, update, aur remove karne deta hai jo Python mein by default included nahi hoti.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **pip = Package Installer for Python**\r\n* **Install → Update → Remove packages** ✅\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n* `pip install numpy`\r\n* `pip install pandas`\r\n* `pip install requests`",
    "question_en": "What is pip?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Pip is Python's package manager used to install, update, and remove external libraries or packages. It helps developers add extra functionality to their Python projects from the Python Package Index (PyPI).\r\n\r\n**Example:**\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npip install requests\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis command installs the `requests` library.\r\n\r\nOther commands:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npip uninstall requests\r\n```\r\n\r\n→ Removes a package\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npip install --upgrade requests\r\n```\r\n\r\n→ Updates a package\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (20 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Pip is a tool used to manage Python packages. It allows us to install, update, and remove third-party libraries that are not included in Python by default.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **pip = Package Installer for Python**\r\n* **Install → Update → Remove packages** ✅\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n* `pip install numpy`\r\n* `pip install pandas`\r\n* `pip install requests`",
