    "category": "Advanced",
    "question_hi": "Multithreading aur multiprocessing mein kya difference hai?",
    "answer_hi": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Multithreading aur multiprocessing ek saath multiple tasks run karne ke tareeke hain, lekin ye differently kaam karte hain. Multithreading ek single process ke andar multiple threads use karta hai aur same memory share karta hai, jabki multiprocessing multiple independent processes use karta hai jinke separate memory spaces hote hain.\r\n\r\n### **Multithreading:**\r\n\r\n> Multiple threads ek process ke andar run hote hain aur resources share karte hain. Ye I/O-bound tasks jaise file operations, network requests, ya waiting tasks ke liye useful hai.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n```python id=\"p8x3vn\"\r\nimport threading\r\n\r\ndef download():\r\n    print(\"Downloading...\")\r\n\r\nt1 = threading.Thread(target=download)\r\nt1.start()\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Multiprocessing:**\r\n\r\n> Multiple processes independently run hote hain, har ek ki apni memory hoti hai. Ye CPU-intensive tasks ke liye useful hai kyunki ye multiple CPU cores use kar sakta hai.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n```python id=\"q4m7za\"\r\nfrom multiprocessing import Process\r\n\r\ndef calculate():\r\n    print(\"Calculating...\")\r\n\r\np1 = Process(target=calculate)\r\np1.start()\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Difference:**\r\n\r\n| Multithreading                   | Multiprocessing                |\r\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\r\n| Ek process mein multiple threads  | Multiple independent processes |\r\n| Memory share karta hai                    | Alag memory                |\r\n| Lightweight aur create karna faster | Zyada resources use karta hai            |\r\n| CPython mein GIL se limited        | GIL bypass karta hai                   |\r\n| I/O-bound tasks ke liye best         | CPU-bound tasks ke liye best       |\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (30 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Multithreading ek single process ke andar multiple threads run karta hai aur mainly I/O-bound tasks ke liye use hota hai. Multiprocessing separate memory ke saath multiple processes create karta hai, jisse true parallel execution possible hota hai aur ye CPU-bound tasks ke liye better hai.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Threads → Same house, shared resources** 🏠\r\n* **Processes → Different houses, independent resources** 🏘️\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\n\r\n* API calls, files download karna → **Multithreading** ✅\r\n* Machine learning training, heavy calculations → **Multiprocessing** ✅",
    "question_en": "What is the difference between multithreading and multiprocessing?",
    "answer_en": "**Interview Answer (Simple English):**\r\n\r\n> Multithreading and multiprocessing are ways to run multiple tasks at the same time, but they work differently. Multithreading uses multiple threads inside a single process and shares the same memory, while multiprocessing uses multiple independent processes with separate memory spaces.\r\n\r\n### **Multithreading:**\r\n\r\n> Multiple threads run inside one process and share resources. It is useful for I/O-bound tasks like file operations, network requests, or waiting tasks.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n```python id=\"p8x3vn\"\r\nimport threading\r\n\r\ndef download():\r\n    print(\"Downloading...\")\r\n\r\nt1 = threading.Thread(target=download)\r\nt1.start()\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Multiprocessing:**\r\n\r\n> Multiple processes run independently, each with its own memory. It is useful for CPU-intensive tasks because it can use multiple CPU cores.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n```python id=\"q4m7za\"\r\nfrom multiprocessing import Process\r\n\r\ndef calculate():\r\n    print(\"Calculating...\")\r\n\r\np1 = Process(target=calculate)\r\np1.start()\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Difference:**\r\n\r\n| Multithreading                   | Multiprocessing                |\r\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\r\n| Multiple threads in one process  | Multiple independent processes |\r\n| Shares memory                    | Separate memory                |\r\n| Lightweight and faster to create | Uses more resources            |\r\n| Limited by GIL in CPython        | Bypasses GIL                   |\r\n| Best for I/O-bound tasks         | Best for CPU-bound tasks       |\r\n\r\n### **Short Version (30 seconds):**\r\n\r\n> Multithreading runs multiple threads within a single process and is mainly used for I/O-bound tasks. Multiprocessing creates multiple processes with separate memory, allowing true parallel execution and is better for CPU-bound tasks.\r\n\r\n💡 **Easy way to remember:**\r\n\r\n* **Threads → Same house, shared resources 🏠**\r\n* **Processes → Different houses, independent resources 🏘️**\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\n\r\n* API calls, downloading files → **Multithreading** ✅\r\n* Machine learning training, heavy calculations → **Multiprocessing** ✅",
